{"kind":"request","text":"Design the complete addressed-work and requester-acceptance lifecycle\n\nBuilder/design: deliver notes/2026-10-03-work-item-lifecycle.md for the full product D1 gap. Distinguish work item, attributable conversation/commitment and leased resource hold. Specify filing before hold with optional scope, addressing, exact-version conditions acceptance, re-addressing while unaccepted, decline, requester withdrawal before/after promise, performer cancellation/release, handover, report, designated requester satisfaction/rejection, non-landing completion/closure, supersession and retained replacement/promise/evidence links. Landing or release is not requester satisfaction. The old claim.hold/claim.to/release.outcome sketches are not adopted. Choose an application repository/declaration model first and show what it can enforce; separately propose any needed unheld opening/closure/guard primitive at an unused amendment number. Include counter-offers and negotiated conditions: identify which conversation transitions the chosen model represents, how changed terms get new explicit actor agreement/version, and which transitions remain unsupported. Never reinterpret an already accepted commitment.\n\nCommissioned under independently approved experience map a259c26d and adopted scope cf116410, planned at main e6e6782830e0ca8a68f0d11c4d4ece5e4e98c967. This request delivers the design/specification and implementing-lane handoff. Planner will commission its implementation separately after exact design review and adoption; no new protocol/runtime decision is adopted here.\n\nReconcile acts-review product D1 and docs-plan D1; review/adopt new semantics. Stage5 and current primitive set are foundations, not proof this lifecycle exists.","body":{"conditions":"Complete actor/state/authority/race/attention tables and two-actor examples, including non-code investigation/report. Specify both race orders for acceptance versus withdrawal/re-address/closure, with lease expiry and policy activation and the reserved-publication boundary. Closed takeover is refused; cancellation never impersonates the requester; decline versus continued open work is explicit. Supply exact implementation lanes and compact fixtures. Independent design review/adoption precedes those separately commissioned lanes. Do not downgrade the full lifecycle to cosmetic body fields. A simpler documented Jam development practice may proceed under builder's actual readiness judgment. Carry a two-agent handover preserving exact conditions and context, and cancellation racing with report/requester acceptance, with both actor/race orders and explicit outcomes.\nDependencies: Reconcile acts-review product D1 and docs-plan D1; review/adopt new semantics. Stage5 and current primitive set are foundations, not proof this lifecycle exists.\nPriority and review: test-overhead ecbc722a remains highest implementation priority, followed by acts and builder-identified concrete Jam blockers. This adds no blanket first-Jam gate. Exact design source artifacts get independent review/adoption before implementing any new choice. Relevant focused checks use the post-ecbc722a workflow; no per-field/per-guard sweeps or numerical test quota.","target_head":"e6e6782830e0ca8a68f0d11c4d4ece5e4e98c967","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}